n found confirming that the building was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami (พ.ศ. 2547) or that it underwent restoration in any particular year. It should therefore not be concluded that it was damaged or repaired because of that event, even though the Takua Pa area has sites connected with tsunami survivor assistance and the old town has regained a cultural-tourism role.</p><p>The old town boundary document by ONEP indicates the boundary passing through Tao Ming School, and the community database of the Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre classifies the building among the important evidence of the old town. However, this search has not yet found a Fine Arts Department announcement directly registering the “Tao Ming School Building”. Therefore, the conservation status of the area is separated from the registration status of the building.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning (ONEP): Takua Pa Old Town Boundary</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>The original building remains in the old town, but it is no longer an active school</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The currently verified status is that the school has closed down, leaving a historical building under the care of the Munlanithi Rongrian Tao Ming Takua Pa (Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation). Therefore, it should be understood that "visiting the building" is not the same as "visiting an operating school".</p><p>The building is located on Thanon Si Takua Pa in the old town area and is still used as a destination in tourism media by the Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality), the Kan Thongthiao Haeng Prathet Thai (Tourism Authority of Thailand), and old town activities, such as the cultural street held in the Thanon Si Takua Pa area. The information found verifies the context of activities in the area but it is not verified that activities are regularly held inside the building.</p><p>The condition verified from official sources is that the building remains and has architectural value in applied Sino-Portuguese style. As for opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access, wheelchair accessibility, and the 2026 (2569 BE) restoration project, there is still no verifiable public information. Therefore, one should contact the caretaker or municipality before traveling.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a> · <a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1099396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">การท่องเที่ยวแห่งประเทศไทย (Tourism Authority of Thailand): TAT Media Assets · Tao Ming School</a> · <a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">องค์การบริหารส่วนจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Administrative Organization): Takua Pa Old Town</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tao Ming School Building (location introduction video)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1920 (2463 BE)</p><h3>Application for Toh Beng Private School</h3><p>The Chinese school, initially operated informally by private individuals, applied for private school status following the Private Schools Act of 1918.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1922 (2465 BE)</p><h3>Construction of Tao Ming School Building</h3><p>The applied Sino-Portuguese building was constructed with donations from tin mining tycoons and Chinese merchants to provide primary and Chinese language education for children in Takua Pa.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1977 to 1986 (2520s BE decade)</p><h3>Decline of the Mining Town</h3><p>Local sources state that tin mines began to gradually close during this decade, reducing the town's vibrancy. However, this is not a verified year for the school's closure.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2020 (2563 BE)</p><h3>Municipality Releases Promotional Video</h3><p>Takua Pa Municipality published a video introducing the Tao Ming School building as an old town tourist attraction.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">21 February 2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School</h3><p>Press releases indicated the Old Town Storytelling event took place at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa. However, full details from primary news sources are not verified.</p><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>School Closes and Foundation Takes Over</h3><p>The exact year of closure is not verified. Official sources state the remaining building is under the care of the Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Old yellow building</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>A historic school building that still remains in the old town area.</p><a href="https://readme.me/p/51787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Applied Sino-Portuguese style</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Observe the building's shape and zinc roof, as noted by conservation agencies.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Traces of Chinese education</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the Takua Pa mining town.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-02-21 · YOUPHUKET</p><h3>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa</h3><p>Press releases reported a full day of activities hosted at Tao Ming School.</p><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>"Toh Beng" is the original name pronounced in the Hokkien dialect, while "Tao Ming" is the Mandarin pronunciation of the name 導明.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>Tao Ming School was the first and only Chinese language school in Takua Pa according to accessible local articles.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The building was constructed by Chinese craftsmen and features a zinc roof in the applied Sino-Portuguese style.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Takua Pa Old Town Community / Talat Yai (Big Market) <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The building was constructed in 1922 (2465 BE). The school started requesting to be established as a private school in 1920 (2463 BE) and originally used the name To Beng according to the Hokkien accent.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A historical school building remaining in the old town area. Observe the building shape and corrugated zinc roof identified by conservation agencies. It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the tin mining town of Takua Pa.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Readme.me: Hello Phang.Nga</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://readme.me/p/51787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">องค์การบริหารส่วนจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Administrative Organization): Takua Pa Old Town</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">การท่องเที่ยวแห่งประเทศไทย (Tourism Authority of Thailand): TAT Media Assets · Tao Ming School</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1099396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tao Ming School Building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">YOUPHUKET: Press release for the Old Town Tells Stories event</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>No building number or postal code found in accessible sources.</li><li>No official opening and closing hours found.</li><li>No admission fee found.</li><li>No official phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account found.</li><li>No verified information on parking, restrooms, and accessibility for wheelchairs or the elderly.</li><li>No information on registration as a historical site by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>No information on individual builders found.</li><li>No festivals held directly at the school found.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>No year of school closure found, nor a list of administrators or teachers.</li><li>No verified evidence of ownership changes or use for other businesses after the school closed.</li><li>No verified evidence that the building was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>No year or documents confirming the specific restoration of the building found.</li><li>No Fine Arts Department announcement directly confirming the registration of the Tao Ming School building as a historical site.</li><li>No opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access permissions, parking, restrooms, or wheelchair access found.</li><li>No verified restoration or development projects for the building in 2026 found.</li><li>No old photos with direct file URLs and clear usage rights found.</li><li>Activity news on February 21, 2026, was found on a PR aggregation page, but the main news or official announcement could not be fully read.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
