ent ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">07</span><span class="event-name">Loy Krathong</span><span class="event-period">Full moon of the 12th Thai lunar month · Document mentions November</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/loy-krathong/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details></div><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
