Park</h1><p class="english">Phra Narai Park</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="phra-narai">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">ดูทริปของคุณ</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/phra-narai.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8696046, 98.3445279 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8696046,98.3445279" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076 421 750 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>The park's origins remain behind a veil of evidence</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>For Phra Narai Public Park itself, no document has been found stating its construction year, initiator, or reason for establishment. It should therefore not be concluded that the park originated in the tin-mining era or during the period of the town governors merely because Takuapa prospered then.</p><p>What can be confirmed is that the park is in front of Takuapa Town Municipality Office and houses a statue of Phra Narai with replicas of attendant deities. Phra Narai is significant to the town and is used in the municipal emblem, but this evidence explains the significance of the deity and the town, not the park's founding date.</p><p>The municipal documents' context for Takuapa reflects an old town with trade, tin mining, Sino·Portuguese buildings, and a large Chinese community. However, no evidence directly connects these elements with the park's construction.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</a> · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a sacred space to a town activity stage</h3><p class="era-years">No verifiable timeline has been found.</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The evidence found does not record any transfer of ownership, abandonment, or restoration of the park over time, so it cannot yet be answered whether the park experienced these events. The same applies to the impact of the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547), for which no report specifically about this park has been found.</p><p>During the period covered by the available information, the park's role expanded from a place of worship to a public space for the town. It is used for cultural activities, recreation, traditional events, Children's Day events, and as a playground, under the management of Takuapa Town Municipality.</p><p>Old-town documents identify several places and ancient monuments in the municipality, but no Fine Arts Department announcement has been found registering “Phra Narai Park Public Garden” directly as an ancient monument. The park is therefore carefully distinguished from nearby ancient monuments.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A public park in the 2026 context</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest publicly available information confirms that the park remains a public space under the care of Takuapa Town Municipality. It contains statues of Phra Narai and attendant deities for worship, as well as a playground and community recreation areas.</p><p>The park also serves as the town's central event stage. The Phra Narai worship ceremony and Takuapa's local products event were held here in 2025 (B.E. 2568), and news reported Takuapa local products activities at the park's central stage. The 2023 (B.E. 2566) annual event was held from 27 March·5 April.</p><p>No official information confirms opening·closing hours, admission fees, the latest physical condition, or a completed construction project. For the “Narai Hub &amp; Commercial Center” development concept, only policy or direction news from municipal administrators has been found, so it is not yet considered a completed project.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath</a> · <a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ThaiPR.NET</a> · <a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Naewna</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">27 March·5 April 2023 (B.E. 2566)</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony</h3><p>The annual event is held at Phra Narai Public Park, along with cultural activities and community products.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2025 (2568 BE)</p><h3>Takua Pa good products fair</h3><p>The central stage of the community economic promotion project was held in the park.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Current status</h3><p>It remains a public park under the municipality's care. It features a worship point, a playground, and an event space.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>The year the park was built has not been found</h3><p>The disclosed documents do not specify the year, founder, or park establishment project.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Phra Narai statue as a city symbol</h3><p>The municipality document states that the Phra Narai statue is sacred to the townspeople and is used as the municipality seal, but does not specify the year it was enshrined in the park.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Phra Narai and attendant statues</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Replicas of the deities enshrined in the park. The originals are ancient sculptures from the Khao Phra Narai archaeological site, now in the Thalang National Museum.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Municipal symbol</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is used as the emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality, reflecting the town's historical roots linked to Indian culture.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Proximity to the Sunday Market</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The park is a landmark near the Takua Pa Old Town Sunday Market, often used as an activity space or gathering point for festivals.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Event area</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Used for municipal cultural activities, recreation, and local traditional events</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-03-14 · ThailandTravel</p><h3>Phra Narai Worship and Takua Pa Good Products Fair 2025 (2568 BE)</h3><p>Announcement scheduling the event for 14·23 March 2025 (B.E. 2568) at the park</p><a href="https://thailandtravel.app/content/read/3344" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2023-03-31 · ThaiPR.NET</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony, an identity of Takua Pa people</h3><p>Report on the 2023 (B.E. 2566) annual event held at the park from 27 March·5 April</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted"> · Siam Rath</p><h3>Takua Pa Town Municipality organised community economic promotion activities, Takua Pa good products</h3><p>Used the park's central stage as the area for the 2025 community economic promotion project.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai statues in the park are replicas; the original ancient sculptures were moved for safekeeping at the Thalang National Museum in Phuket.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is the official emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The park is managed by Takuapa Town Municipality. It is a place for recreation and houses statues of Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A Phra Narai devotional sculpture is available for public worship. According to official sources, the park contains Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities, and part of the park is a playground.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cultural Information Centre (m-culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AAาธารณะอุทยานพระนารายณ์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phang Nga Primary Educational Service Area Office</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ThaiPR.NET</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9550000099132" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Published and verified opening hours are not verified.</li><li>Admission fee data is not verified.</li><li>Current conditions of facilities like restrooms, parking, and wheelchair accessibility are not verified for 2026.</li><li>The specific schedule for the annual Phra Narai worship ceremony is not confirmed.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>No information on the construction year or builder has been found.</li><li>No evidence confirming the park's role during the tin-mining era has been found.</li><li>No evidence was found confirming Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture at the garden</li><li>No evidence was found that the garden is registered as an ancient monument</li><li>No nearby places with a verified walking distance were found</li><li>No verified event month or lunar calendar information was found</li><li>The garden's construction year and builder</li><li>The garden's original purpose or founding project</li><li>The history of ownership changes, abandonment, or restoration</li><li>Evidence of impact from the 2004 tsunami ( พ.ศ. 2547 )</li><li>The year the garden itself was registered as an ancient monument</li><li>Opening and closing hours · admission fee · latest condition of the buildings and structures</li><li>Whether the Narai Hub project is actually underway</li><li>No old image explicitly identified as showing the garden has been found</li><li>No direct URL for a current image file with verifiable usage rights has been found</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
