"url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-pathum/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/wat-pathum.webp", "description": "โบสถ์เก่าและเรื่องการขนส่งทางน้ำเชื่อมสถานที่นี้กับประวัติการค้าของเมือง", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนหน้าเมือง ชุมชนตลาดใหญ่", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8282064, "longitude": 98.3667554}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · เว็บเลิฟไทยแลนด์ระบุทุกวัน 08.00·17.00 น. ยังไม่มีประกาศจากวัดยืนยัน"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เอกสารเทศบาลระบุว่าอุโบสถเป็นศิลปะพื้นถิ่นภาคใต้และใช้เสาไม้เป็นแกน เทศบาลระบุว่ากรมศิลปากรขึ้นทะเบียนอุโบสถเป็นโบราณสถานใน พ.ศ. 2478; การวิจัยครั้งนี้ยังไม่ได้ตรวจประกาศขึ้นทะเบียนต้นฉบับ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "รายละเอียดโครงสร้างที่เอกสารเทศบาลกล่าวถึง เหมาะกับการสังเกตงานช่างพื้นถิ่น; ยังไม่มีข้อมูลว่ามองเห็นได้ครบจากภายนอกหรือไม่ ชิ้นส่วนเรือที่แหล่งข้อมูลระบุว่าจัดอยู่ในบริเวณวัด เป็นหลักฐานเชื่อมกับการขนส่งสินค้าทางน้ำของเมือง ทั้งนี้ยังไม่มีข้อมูลตรวจสภาพล่าสุดในปี 2569"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-pathum/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-pathum/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-pathum/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">เรื่องเล่า</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">แผ่นพับ</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/wat-pathum/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Temples & Pagodas</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Temples and pagodas</span><h1>Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</h1><p class="english">Wat Pathum Thara</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">8 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="wat-pathum">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">ดูทริปของคุณ</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/wat-pathum.webp" alt="วัดปทุมธารา (วัดหน้าเมือง)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8282064, 98.3667554 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8282064,98.3667554" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/815944559" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>LoveThailand website indicates everyday 08.00·17.00 hrs. There is no verified announcement from the temple yet. <span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://www.lovethailand.org/travel/en/68-Phang-Nga/7958-Wat-Na-Mueang.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>Wat Na Mueang and the restoration of Takua Pa</h3><p class="era-years">1777 (2320 BE) or during the town's revival in the reign of King Rama III (still debated)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>The origins of Wat Pathum Thara or Wat Na Mueang are told in two ways. Tesaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality) records the oral history that Lady Thao, daughter of Phraya Takua Pa (Muang), built the temple in 1777 (2320 BE). However, the ONEP old town database explains that after the old town was destroyed and abandoned during the Burmese war, the town's revival at Ban Talat Yai in the reign of King Rama III started with the construction of Wat Na Mueang, followed by the governor's residence nearby.</p><p>The big picture of Takua Pa is a riverine port town and a center for the tin trade. The town prospered from mining and maritime trade. Chinese laborers, especially Hokkien Chinese, settled and connected the culture with the Malay Peninsula. The temple likely served as the main religious site of the Talat Yai community and a landmark for the newly establishing town, but found sources do not identify a confirmed builder or its daily ritual roles in that era.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Takua Pa Old Town</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai</a> · <a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a water port to an old town district</h3><p class="era-years">1867·1956 (2410·2499 BE) and 1935 (2478 BE)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>During the era of water trade, the temple was near areas with traffic and goods transport. Community sources indicate that a boiler in the temple grounds is a part of a steamboat that Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch na Nakhon) co-invested to buy in 1867 (2410 BE) to transport goods and suppress pirates, before the boat deteriorated and sank in the Takua Pa River. This evidence reflects trade networks but is not evidence that the temple operated mining businesses itself.</p><p>When the town center moved to Ban Yan Yao in 1913 (2456 BE) and waterways became shallow, Ban Talat Yai's economic role declined. The temple remained a religious site and community space. The temple's monks' living quarters were initially used as classrooms for Rongrian Tesaban Ban Si Takua Pa (Ban Si Takua Pa Municipal School) before the school moved to its current location in 1956 (2499 BE). The municipality notes that the southern vernacular ordination hall was registered as an ancient monument in 1935 (2478 BE), but the original announcement has not been checked in this research phase.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai</a> · <a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/English-school-Takuapa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">วารสารเมืองโบราณ (Muang Boran Journal): The first English school in Takua Pa</a> · <a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A religious site in the Talat Yai community whose status requires on-site checking</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The verified information confirms the temple's location on Thanon Na Mueang in the Talat Yai community and confirms the value of the old ordination hall as a heritage of the old town. However, no official announcements or news in the last 5 years have been found that confirm restoration projects, regular activities, or direct visiting conditions of the temple.</p><p>A travel website states opening hours as 08:00·17:00 daily, yet there are no confirmed announcements from the temple or government agencies. It should be considered unverified information, and contacting the area before traveling is recommended. Access inside the ordination hall, the condition of the boiler, caretaking by the monastic community, and community activities in 2026 (2569 BE) remain issues that require field surveys.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</a> · <a href="https://www.lovethailand.org/travel/th/68-%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%B2/7958-%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B7%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%87.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Love Thailand: Wat Na Mueang</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">1777 (2320 BE)</p><h3>Tale of the Temple's Construction</h3><p>The municipality records a tale that Than Thao, daughter of Phraya Takua Pa (Muang), built Wat Na Mueang this year, but another set of evidence links the temple to the town's revival during King Rama III's reign.</p><a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1867 (2410 BE)</p><h3>Steamboat and the Takua Pa River</h3><p>The steam boiler in the temple area is linked to a steamboat used to transport goods and suppress pirates, co-purchased by Phraya Senanuchit and Phraya Wichit Songkhram.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1935 (2478 BE)</p><h3>Ordination Hall Registered as a Historical Site</h3><p>The municipality notes that the Fine Arts Department registered the ordination hall, but the original announcement is not verified.</p><a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1956 (2499 BE)</p><h3>Monk Cells as Initial Classrooms</h3><p>The Ban Si Takua Pa Municipal School once held classes in the temple's monk cells before moving to its current location.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/English-school-Takuapa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Town Revival at Ban Talat Yai</h3><p>The ONEP database states that the construction of the new town began with building Wat Na Mueang before constructing the governor's residence nearby.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Old ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>See the religious building that the municipality identifies as southern art and registered as a historical site. It is not verified if the interior is open on visit days.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Wooden core pillars of the ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Structural details mentioned in municipal documents, suitable for observing local craftsmanship. It is not verified whether they are fully visible from the outside.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Steamboat boiler</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>A boat part that sources say is kept within the temple grounds, serving as evidence linked to the town's water transport. Its latest condition in 2026 is not verified.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The steam boiler in the temple grounds is said to be a part of a steamboat used to transport goods and suppress pirates in 1867.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The temple's monk quarters were once used as an early classroom for the Ban Si Takua Pa Municipal School.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/English-school-Takuapa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Not verified · The Love Thailand website states daily 08:00·17:00. Still no confirmed announcement from the temple.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Municipal documents indicate that the ordination hall is of southern vernacular art and uses wooden pillars as its core. The municipality notes that Krom Sinlapakon (Fine Arts Department) registered the ordination hall as an ancient monument in 1935 (2478 BE); this research has not yet checked the original registration announcement.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>The structural details mentioned in the municipal documents are suitable for observing vernacular craftsmanship; there is no information yet on whether it is fully visible from the outside. The boat part, which sources indicate is located in the temple grounds, is evidence connected to the town's water transport of goods. However, there is no latest condition check information in 2026 (2569 BE).</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Tesaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan for Fiscal Year 2020 (2563 BE), pages 11·12</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Talat Yai</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Takua Pa Old Town</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal: English School at Takua Pa during the reign of King Rama V</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/English-school-Takuapa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Love Thailand: Wat Na Mueang</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.lovethailand.org/travel/en/68-Phang-Nga/7958-Wat-Na-Mueang.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">วารสารเมืองโบราณ (Muang Boran Journal): The first English school in Takua Pa</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/English-school-Takuapa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Love Thailand: Wat Na Mueang</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.lovethailand.org/travel/th/68-%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%B2/7958-%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%99%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%B2%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B7%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%87.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>GPS coordinates are not verified from Google Maps, OpenStreetMap, Mapcarta, or Wikidata.</li><li>Address: The road name and entrance should be checked on-site. House numbers are not verified.</li><li>The English name uses the name set by the employer. An official English name is not verified.</li><li>Opening hours are only found on travel websites and old data. Current schedules or ordination hall opening times are not verified.</li><li>Admission fees, phone numbers, Facebook pages, websites, and LINE accounts of the temple are not verified.</li><li>Travel methods from Takua Pa town, Phuket, and Khao Lak are not verified.</li><li>Founding year and builder: Primary evidence to decide this is not verified.</li><li>Registration: The original announcement, volume, part, date, and land boundaries are not verified.</li><li>Role in the tin mining era: Evidence that the temple owned mines or was directly an ore port is not verified.</li><li>Chinese or Sino-Portuguese architecture of the temple: Specific evidence for the temple buildings is not verified.</li><li>Recommended visit times, duration, and specific dress codes for the temple are not verified.</li><li>Temple-specific festivals, months, lunar calendar dates, and activities are not verified.</li><li>Parking, restrooms, ramps, and accessibility for the elderly or wheelchairs are not verified.</li><li>Nearby places within walking distance are not verified.</li><li>Official images with verified rights are not verified.</li><li>The current condition or access to the ordination hall, wooden pillar details, and the steam boiler are not verified.</li><li>The verified founding year and builder still conflict between the 1777 account and the story of the town's revival in the reign of King Rama III.</li><li>A Royal Gazette announcement or original Fine Arts Department database confirming the 1935 registration is not verified.</li><li>Evidence confirming direct impacts from the 2004 tsunami is not verified.</li><li>News from the past 5 years specifically matching the temple, or renovation/development projects during that period, are not verified.</li><li>Direct image URLs for the temple with verifiable credits and rights are not verified.</li><li>It is not verified whether the temple currently opens its ordination hall for viewing, what the interior condition is like, and what regular activities exist.</li><li>The name of the temple caretaker or the latest renovation data is not verified.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\traditions\chak-phra\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Chak Phra Festival · Phang Nga Chak Phra · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="A community event that connects faith with a procession · Khura Buri Chak Phra · Southern Thailand Buddhist festival"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Chak Phra Festival · Phang Nga Chak Phra"><meta property="og:description" content="A community event that connects faith with a procession · Khura Buri Chak Phra · Southern Thailand Buddhist festival"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/traditions/chak-phra/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/chak-phra.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/chak-phra.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/traditions/chak-phra/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Chak Phra Tradition", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/traditions/chak-phra/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "Event", "name": "Chak Phra Tradition", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/traditions/chak-phra/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/chak-phra.png", "description": "Pulling the Buddha boat out of the temple · Buddha boat contest · Performances from each temple · Buddha boat celebration · Cultural performances", "location": {"@type": "Place", "name": "Khura Buri District Office, Phang Nga (the source information states this, not Takua Pa)"}}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/traditions/chak-phra/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/traditions/chak-phra/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/traditions/chak-phra/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">เรื่องเล่า</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" aria-current="page" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">แผ่นพับ</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/traditions/chak-phra/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>Chak Phra Festival</h1><p class="lead">Day after Buddhist Lent ends</p></div><div class="event-note"><span class="calendar-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><article><span class="chapter">Periods from document</span><h2>Day after Buddhist Lent ends</h2><p>This item appears in the activities and traditions section of the Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure. The period above is not yet a verified schedule for the current year.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/">View year-round traditions ↗</a></article></div><section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">Read more / Open town stories</span><h2>Related places</h2></div><p></p></div><div class="related-grid"><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดบรมธาตุคีรีเขต (วัดลุ่ม)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/"><img src="/assets/wat-boromthat.webp" alt="วัดบรมธาตุคีรีเขต (วัดลุ่ม)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">01</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidde